-- title:
--   The information before the reward of round $t$
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal H_s$ be the information available after round $s$ and $\pi^t$ the decision of round $t$. This is the $\sigma$-algebra $\mathcal H_{t-1}\vee\sigma(\pi^t)$ generated by the past and the current decision. The reward $r^t$ is drawn conditionally on it in Assumption 4.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Rounds are $1,\dots,T$, so $t-1$ is the usual predecessor on every round used.
-- source:
--   Foster & Rakhlin, Foundations of Reinforcement Learning and Interactive Decision Making, arXiv:2312.16730v1, Assumption 4, (4.1), and the history, p. 57

import Mathlib

open MeasureTheory

namespace FoundationsRL.EluderUCB

/-- **The information just before the reward of round `t`.** The σ-algebra generated by the
history through round `t - 1` and the decision `πᵗ`: the conditioning of Assumption 4, Foster &
Rakhlin, arXiv:2312.16730v1, (4.1), p. 57, and of the history `Hᵗ` defined there.

**Formalization Note.** `𝓗 s` is the information after round `s`. Rounds are `1, …, T`, so `t - 1`
is honest natural-number subtraction on every round used; `t = 0` does not occur. -/
abbrev preRewardSigma {Ω Act : Type*} {mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω} [MeasurableSpace Act]
    (𝓗 : Filtration ℕ mΩ) (π : ℕ → Ω → Act) (t : ℕ) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  𝓗 (t - 1) ⊔ MeasurableSpace.comap (π t) inferInstance

end FoundationsRL.EluderUCB


